+
+Self-serve positive controls held throughout the same cycle: `system_health`,
+`bridge.work_queue`, `bridge.work_order`, `work_claim` (GRANT_RENEW) all reachable.
+
+## 4. The upgrade: "predates" is dead, "diverges" is the only survivor
+
+Pass 3's conclusion was deliberately two-branched: *"the running build predates or
+diverges from the in-repo SSOT"*. Pass 4 kills the first branch. The deployment
+demonstrably changed (new tools exist and execute; a restart was witnessed by the
+independent watchdog plane), yet four of the five flagged tools still execute
+anonymously and the positive control still walks zod → RBAC → vendor handler. A rebuild
+that consumes `infrastructure/mcp-control-plane/src/policy/mcp-access.ts` cannot ship
+`marketplace_*` tools AND retain the anonymous five unless `classifyToolCapability` is
+not wired into the runtime gate at all. The evidence now supports the stronger claim:
+**the deployed build pipeline is not consuming the in-repo SSOT policy** (or deploys an
+artifact that never binds it). The source-side guard (`mcp_access_policy_guard.py`, wired
+into `run_all_guards.py`) keeps the mirror honest while the deployment floats free —
+exactly the gap the ADMIN RECIPE exists to close, and the recipe has now survived one
+full redeploy cycle unexecuted.
+
+## 5. github_list_secrets disposition: removal is not the prescribed pin
+
+The R4 tool is gone from both advertisement and execution. In practice the #1843 leak
+for this tool is closed — an anonymous caller can no longer enumerate secret names
+through it. But the SSOT prescribes a **pin** (restricted + secret classification block,
+enforced by `SECRET_FAMILY_EXPLICIT` in the guard), not absence. Two readings:
+
+1. The policy IS consumed and deliberately drops the tool — then the other four
+   tools' persistence contradicts the same pipeline consuming the same file, so this
+   reading requires two different build behaviors in one deploy. Unlikely.
+2. The tool was dropped upstream of the policy (registry/handler split — the same
+   dotted/underscore registry-split class documented in #2722 and #2751/#2764), and the
+   classification pin never got a chance to apply.
+
+Under either reading, the guard's expectation (pinned AND denied) is not what is
+deployed, and the guard stays green because it audits the source, not the deployment.
+The disposition question (re-register the tool under the pin, or amend the SSOT to
+codify its removal) is a maintainer decision this receipt surfaces but does not make.
+
+## 6. New-surface classification (marketplace, first anonymous pass)
+
+- `marketplace_list_plugins`: readOnly + idempotent annotations; returned 5 catalog
+  templates (3,046B). The advertisement text itself carries the #1843-class contract —
+  "credential fields are SPECS (names/labels), never values" — and the shape-classified
+  response is consistent with a templates-only catalog.
+- `marketplace_list_connections`: an anonymous, tenant-less call **executes** (not
+  denied), returning `count: 0`. No cross-tenant rows were witnessed this pass, but the
+  tool sits in the credential-adjacent family and its anonymous executability is the
+  same drift class as the flagged five: a call that should die at RBAC instead reaches
+  the handler and returns a well-formed (empty) payload. Recommendation: add it — and
+  each future credential-adjacent tool at advertisement time — to the deny-matrix probe
+  set, so the matrix grows with the surface instead of trailing it.
+
+## 7. Maintainer asks (recipe unchanged; one addition)
+
+1. The ADMIN RECIPE (rebuild + redeploy + anonymous deny-matrix probe expecting
+   Forbidden on all five) remains the closure path — now with sharper evidence for its
+   step 1: a rebuild+redeploy happened between pass 3 and pass 4 **without** reconciling,
+   so verify the pipeline linkage itself — confirm the deployed artifact actually builds
+   from `infrastructure/mcp-control-plane` and that `classifyToolCapability` is bound
+   into the runtime gate rather than only mirror-checked by the source-side guard.
+2. Decide the `github_list_secrets` disposition (§5): re-register under the pin, or
+   amend the SSOT to codify removal.
+3. Extend the deny-matrix probe set with credential-adjacent newcomers (§6).
+4. The optional secret-name rotation (recipe step 4) remains moot while
+   `github_list_secrets` is absent, but the 26-entity memory graph (§3) is itself an
+   unexamined disclosure surface — its contents were not captured this pass and should
+   be classified by an authenticated operator.
+
